{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Behold I have given you.</b> I am now giving to you — in לשון הזה (Old French) <i>dunai</i> (I give). And similarly, 'I have lifted My hand' — I am lifting. 'I have given silver for the field' — I am giving." "<b>All herb of seed seed.</b> Such as grain and legumes and the fruit of the tree — these are for human food. But to every beast of the field I have given all green herb, such as cabbage, spinach, and similar things. And when man sinned, it was decreed upon him to eat herb, as it is written, 'and thorn and thistle etc.', and 'you shall eat the herb of the field' — this is what is meant by 'compared to beasts he is likened' — for if meat were permitted to him, we would find a sinner rewarded." "<b>To you it shall be for food…and to every beast of the earth.</b> Rashi equated for them the domesticated and wild animals and did not permit them to eat meat. And this is what is in chapter Four Deaths: the ministering angels strain wine for him and roast meat for him — that is meat that descends from heaven. And what is written, 'and rule over the fish of the sea' — that is for labor, as Reḥava requires: he led a goat and a kid — what of it? And 'the bird of the heavens' — that is for labor, as Rava bar Rav Huna requires: a goose and a rooster — what of it? And 'every creature that creeps upon the earth' — that is a snake for an errand, as is stated in chapter Four Deaths."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The Old French gloss reads דונאץ in the Hebrew, here rendered as 'I give' based on Chizkuni's own parenthetical gloss נותן אני. The exact Old French form cited may reflect a present-tense donor/don.", 2 "The Talmudic references are to Sanhedrin 59b (the heavenly meat passage and the snake-as-messenger). The term פרש״י is given as 'Rashi' per the voice rules, even though Chizkuni's compiler typically does not name sources — here he himself names this source explicitly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:20:19.246721341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}